        { "id": "recipe_ndole", "type": "image", "recipeId": "ndole", "recipeName": "Ndolè", "link": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Ndol%C3%A9_camerounais.JPG/960px-Ndol%C3%A9_camerounais.JPG", "caption": "*Ndolè* 🌳 Cameroon's national dish\n\n📋 *Ingredients:*\n• Ndolè leaves (washed & dried) — from AfroMarket\n• White peanuts (arachide blanche) — from AfroMarket\n• Beef, smoked fish and/or shrimp (bring your own)\n• 2 onions, garlic, crayfish, palm oil (bring your own)\n• Fufu: cassava or plantain, pounded (bring your own)\n\n👨‍🍳 *Steps:*\n1. Cook meat/fish with onions and garlic; keep the stock.\n2. Blend the peanuts and simmer in the stock 15 min.\n3. Add the rehydrated Ndolè leaves, crayfish and shrimp; cook 15 min.\n4. Fry garnish onions in oil, fold in; serve with hot fufu.\n\n⏱ 55 min | 🔥 ~490 kcal | 💪 Medium", "next": "recipe_actions" },

